    "Lumen Viae" : {

    },
    "LUMEN VIAE" : {

    },
    "Lumen Viae helps you pray the Rosary each day, with a short reading for every mystery, and keeps the Church's other prayers close at hand. The mysteries are scenes from the lives of Jesus and Mary: the Joyful, Sorrowful, Glorious and Luminous, and the Seven Sorrows of Mary." : {
      "comment" : "About Lumen Viae: a section's text"
    },
    "Lumen Viae is made by one person, for the greater glory of God. If a credit here is wrong or missing, write through Send Feedback and it will be put right." : {

    },
    "Lumen Viae v%@" : {

    },
    "LUMEN VIAE V%@" : {

    },
    "Luminous on Thursday, Joyful on Saturday" : {
      "comment" : "Settings, Daily Mysteries: the two days on which this schedule differs; Joyful, Glorious and Luminous are sets of mysteries"
    },
    "Make a new set" : {

    },
    "Make full width" : {

    },
    "Make half width" : {

    },
    "Make sure notifications are enabled for Lumen Viae in your iPhone's Settings → Notifications. Then toggle Daily Reminders off and back on in the app to reschedule." : {
      "comment" : "Help & Support: the answer to the question above it; names of buttons and settings must match the app's own words"
    },
    "Make your own set" : {

    },
    "Marian Blue" : {
      "comment" : "Settings, App Icon: the name of an icon\nSettings, Appearance: the name of a color theme"
    },
    "Meditation" : {
      "comment" : "Strand margin, said aloud: the bead is named for the meditation being read"
    },
    "Meditation Only" : {
      "comment" : "A Rosary choice's option, short, set in a two-part pill: Audio is Meditation Only, Read in Silence or Whole Rosary; Counting is On My Rosary or On the Screen"
    },
    "Meditations" : {
      "comment" : "Mysteries' page: heading over the shelf of meditation sets"
    },
    "Meditations and audio will stream when you're online. You can download everything again at any time." : {

    },
    "Meditations come from our server. If you're offline, or they haven't been added yet, some meditations may not be available. Check your internet connection and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Help & Support: the answer to the question above it; names of buttons and settings must match the app's own words"
    },
    "Meditations, narration, the Hours of Prayer (the Divine Office), the words of the prayers, and the chants' recordings and sheet music come from our own server; the Mass texts from Missale Meum; the books and recordings under Spiritual Reading from Project Gutenberg and LibriVox. Each receives the request itself, as any website does, and nothing more. The app carries no analytics or advertising code from anyone else, and nothing is used to track you." : {
      "comment" : "Privacy Policy: a section's text; keep it as plain and exact as the English"
    },
    "Memorare" : {
      "comment" : "Settings, After the Rosary: name of a prayer said after the Rosary\nShort name of a prayer said after the Rosary, for a summary line"
    },
    "Midnight" : {
      "comment" : "Settings, App Icon: the name of an icon\nSettings, Appearance: the name of a color theme"
    },
    "MILESTONE REACHED" : {

    },
    "Milestones Ahead" : {

    },
    "MINUTES OF SILENCE" : {

    },
    "Miss a day? Every day stays open. Return whenever you can." : {

