      "comment" : "VoiceOver: a switch is on"
    },
    "On %@" : {

    },
    "On each of the next three small beads, a Hail Mary. This first one asks God for an increase of faith." : {
      "comment" : "Guided Rosary: what to do on the first of the three small beads, a Hail Mary for faith"
    },
    "On each, the Glory Be and the Fatima Prayer close one decade; then the next mystery is announced, and its Our Father said on the same bead." : {
      "comment" : "How to Pray, the beads lesson: what is prayed on this part of the rosary"
    },
    "On My Rosary" : {
      "comment" : "A Rosary choice's option, short, set in a two-part pill: Audio is Meditation Only, Read in Silence or Whole Rosary; Counting is On My Rosary or On the Screen"
    },
    "On the home screen, tap the sliders at the top left, then Prayer Experience → Text Size. Drag the slider toward the larger \"A\" to increase the meditation text size." : {
      "comment" : "Help & Support: the answer to the question above it; names of buttons and settings must match the app's own words"
    },
    "On the large bead, the Our Father." : {
      "comment" : "Guided Rosary: what to do on each later decade's Our Father"
    },
    "On the large bead, the Our Father. Keep the scene before you as you pray." : {
      "comment" : "Guided Rosary: what to do on the first decade's Our Father"
    },
    "On the next large bead, before its Our Father, close the decade." : {
      "comment" : "Guided Rosary: what to do when the second, third or fourth decade closes"
    },
    "On the Screen" : {
      "comment" : "A Rosary choice's option, short, set in a two-part pill: Audio is Meditation Only, Read in Silence or Whole Rosary; Counting is On My Rosary or On the Screen"
    },
    "Once opened, this book reads offline." : {

    },
    "One short note, when you finish a Rosary prayed with meditations: which meditations they were, and whether you listened to the Whole Rosary. Our server keeps it with the time and an approximate city, region and country, looked up through ipapi.co from the address your phone connects from, and keeps that address only in a shortened form. No name, account or device identifier goes with it, so two Rosaries prayed on one phone look like two prayed by strangers. We use these notes only to learn which meditations are prayed, and roughly where. The Scriptural Rosary, the Audio Rosary and the guided Rosary send nothing, and nothing else reaches us unless you write to us." : {
      "comment" : "Privacy Policy: a section's text; keep it as plain and exact as the English"
    },
    "One verse of Scripture for every Hail Mary." : {
      "comment" : "The Scriptural Rosary's own page: the italic line under its name"
    },
    "One warm tone with a soft shimmer" : {
      "comment" : "Settings, Reminder Sound: what the sound is like"
    },
    "Open a mystery to see its meditation sets, each under its own painting. The filter button shows only the kinds you choose, and a set you pin stays at the top. You can read each meditation, or listen when a set has narration." : {

    },
